<===> README.md
User defined functions and mixins that recurse without end must fail with an
error instead of overflowing the native stack (dart-sass crashes with an
uncaught "Stack Overflow"). Finite recursion of a few hundred levels works.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> function/input.scss
@function f($n) {@return f($n + 1)}
a {b: f(0)}
<===> function/error
Error: Too deep recursion detected. This can be caused by too deep level nesting.
LibSass will abort here in order to avoid a possible stack overflow.
  ,
1 | @function f($n) {@return f($n + 1)}
  |                          ^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:26  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> mixin/input.scss
@mixin m {@include m}
a {@include m}
<===> mixin/error
Error: Too deep recursion detected. This can be caused by too deep level nesting.
LibSass will abort here in order to avoid a possible stack overflow.
  ,
1 | @mixin m {@include m}
  |           ^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:11  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> content/input.scss
@mixin m {@include m {@content}}
a {@include m {b: c}}
<===> content/error
Error: Too deep recursion detected. This can be caused by too deep level nesting.
LibSass will abort here in order to avoid a possible stack overflow.
  ,
1 | @mixin m {@include m {@content}}
  |           ^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:11  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> deep_but_finite/input.scss
@function f($n) {@if $n <= 0 {@return 0} @return f($n - 1) + 1}
a {b: f(500)}
<===> deep_but_finite/output.css
a {
  b: 500;
}
